maria: Heads up — hitting a weird break on a Next edge deploy. App fails with `Unexpected token 'export'` when requiring the SDK from an edge route. Works fine on serverless node. Anyone seen this?
ashwin: Yea this smells like ESM/CJS exports mismatch for edge builds. Which SDK version and how are you importing it?
maria: Using redwood-client v0.3.2 (installed yesterday). Import is `import { createClient } from 'redwood-client'` in an edge route. Next build succeeds, but runtime error on Vercel edge at request time.
sam: Two quick checks: 1) Did you set "type":"module" anywhere? 2) Are you bundling node_modules or externalizing the SDK? Next sometimes leaves a raw ESM in the bundle.
maria: No module type set. We're not transpiling node_modules. Next config uses `experimental: { runtime: 'edge' }` per-route.
nora: If the published package only ships ESM entrypoints, Vercel's edge runtime expects pure web-compatible modules. If Next didn't bundle it into the final edge bundle, the runtime may see `export` that it's not prepared for.
ashwin: Possible fixes: - publish a CJS fallback in package.json exports or - ensure Next bundles the package (transpile). For Next 13+, try `transpilePackages: ['redwood-client']` in next.config.js or add an ESM->CJS build for the SDK.
jeff: Also check the `exports` in the SDK's package.json. Something like:
```json
{"exports": {"./package.json": "./package.json", ".": {"import": "dist/index.mjs", "require": "dist/index.cjs"}}}
```
If only `import` is present edge/runtime may choke depending on bundle.
sam: For a quick workaround in your app, you can force bundling by importing the actual file: `import createClient from 'redwood-client/dist/index.mjs'` (not ideal) or add `transpilePackages`.
maria: Streaming is another problem we noticed — after we patched the import, streaming responses from the SDK's `streamChat` in edge return a Node Readable instead of a WHATWG ReadableStream. Edge expects web streams so we get `TypeError: response.body.getReader is not a function`.
nora: Oof. The SDK currently exposes Node-style streams in some builds. We need a web-streams compatible path for edge builds. For now, convert Node stream to a web stream in the app: `new Response(stream)` won't work unless it's a web ReadableStream.
ashwin: Quick converter snippet if you need it temporarily:
```js
// node-stream -> web ReadableStream
function nodeToWeb(nodeStream){
  const reader = nodeStream.getReader ? nodeStream.getReader() : null;
  if (reader) return nodeStream; // already web stream
  const rs = new ReadableStream({
    start(controller){
      nodeStream.on('data', chunk => controller.enqueue(chunk));
      nodeStream.on('end', () => controller.close());
      nodeStream.on('error', err => controller.error(err));
    }
  });
  return rs;
}
```
jeff: We're planning a patch to publish a web-streams build and add a CJS bundle for node consumers. I can prep a release candidate today.
maria: That'd help. Also: auth retries behave differently on edge — our retry middleware uses `setTimeout` which isn't present in some edge contexts. Got flaky 401->refresh loops.
sam: Use `globalThis.setTimeout` or a queue-based backoff that doesn't depend on timers in edge. Or handle auth at upstream and pass short-lived tokens to the edge route.
nora: We'll also add a note in the SDK README about edge compatibility: ESM, web-streams, and no reliance on Node built-ins.
jeff: PR incoming: #2345 — includes: package.json conditional exports, dist/index.cjs, dist/index.mjs, and a `dist/index.web.mjs` that uses web-streams and avoids node deps. Assigning @ashwin @nora for review.
ashwin: I'll review after lunch. If we merge, can we cut a patch release and tag `edge-compatible` in the changelog?
jeff: Yep. I'll add a migration note and a small migration snippet for Next/Vite: `next.config.js` -> `transpilePackages: ['redwood-client']` and for Vite `optimizeDeps.include = ['redwood-client']` + `ssr.noExternal = ['redwood-client']`.
maria: Thanks team — I'll try the transpile workaround and add the node->web stream shim in the meantime. Please ping here when RC is published. :pray:
